      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "$-50-50=$",
      "worked_solution": "The answer will be negative since $-50$ is negative, and we're subtracting $50$ from it.\n\nWe start by solving an easier problem:\n\n$$\n50+50\n$$\n\nNext, we carry out the addition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\text{ }1\\,\\,\\,\\, &  &  \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n50+50=100.\n$$\n\nHowever, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above. \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n-50-50=-100.\n$$",
